:0.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.1778120184899846,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":95.3,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.07603031649416404,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":92.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.07573356897121325,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":0.09242714321409604,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":46.2,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.8137028442100461,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.00851063829787234,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":13.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.05474198727169636,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":15.1,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.06563789772534023,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":57.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.030454801105164186,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":40.2,"_gate_margins":0.006853019459237564,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":56.9,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.10925434480257493,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.05144147169477031,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007027615559734733,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":88.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.011410001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Owens Corning provides residential and commercial building products in the United States, Europe, the Asia Pacific, and internationally. It operates through three segments: Roofing, Insulation, and Doors. The company offers laminate and strip asphalt roofing shingles, roofing components, and oxidized asphalt. It also provides high, mid, and low temperature products; thermal and acoustical batts, loosefill insulation, spray foam insulation, wet use chopped strand, foam sheathing and accessories under the Owens Corning PINK, Next Gen, and FIBERGLAS Insulation brands; and glass fiber pipe insulation, energy efficient flexible duct media, bonded and granulated stone wool insulation, and cellular glass insulation and foam insulation under the FOAMULAR, FOAMGLAS, and Paroc brand names. In addition, the company offers residential interior and exterior doors; glass, fiberglass and metal, and door components such as frames, sills, weather-stripping, hinges and locks. Further, it manufactures, fabricates, and sells glass reinforcements in the form of fiber and mats. The company distributes its products to distributors, home centers and lumberyards, installers, retailers, homebuilders, contractors, dealers, building products retailers, and remodeling contractors. Owens Corning was incorporated in 1938 and is headquartered in Toledo, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian D. Chambers | CEO & Chair | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 25K people. Revenue per employee of $404K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $38K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Owens Corning Inc is a mid-cap industrials business with a $9.6B market cap on $10.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 8% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 23% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $962M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 104% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 32% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Valued at a 38% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Most-Watched Stock Owens Corning Inc (OC) Worth Betting on Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3035027/is-most-watched-stock-owens-corning-inc-oc-worth-betting-on-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cmost_searched_stocks_v1-3035027","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795611604.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Festive Fun Begins November 27 as Winter Fest OC Kicks off its 12th Season","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/festive-fun-begins-november-27-as-winter-fest-oc-kicks-off-its-12th-season-302948566.html","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795461420.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.904,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Owens Corning Inc New (OC) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/20/How_Owens_Corning_Inc_New_OC_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_112226065601_1795391761.html","date":"2026-11-22","timestamp":1795391761.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"5,374 Shares in Owens Corning Inc $OC Bought by Maryland State Retirement & Pension System","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/5374-shares-in-owens-corning-inc-oc-bought-by-maryland-state-retirement-pension-system.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795171252.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Owens Corning (OC) Stock Looks Below Fair Value On Cash Flow","sou